<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ilorin Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1823 CE – 1897 CE (approx.) · capital Ilorin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Yoruba-speaking emirate of the Sokoto Caliphate, born from a revolt against the Oyo Empire, whose rise helped bring about Oyo's collapse.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin</a> was a frontier town of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>. Around 1817 its commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonja">Afonja</a>, holding the military title Are Ona Kakanfo, rebelled against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaafin">Alaafin</a>, relying on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> cleric <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shehu-alimi">Shehu Alimi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> Muslim fighters. After Alimi's death his son Abdulsalami turned on Afonja, killed him around 1823, and became the first emir under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gwandu-emirate">Gwandu Emirate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin's</a> cavalry raided deep into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorubaland">Yorubaland</a> and helped destroy the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> capital in the 1830s, but <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ibadan">Ibadan</a> defeated it at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osogbo">Osogbo</a> around 1840, halting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a>'s advance south. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> combined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> rulers, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a> residents, and became a centre of Islamic learning, crafts such as pottery and weaving, and trade between the savanna and the forest.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin</a> fought in the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> wars against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ekiti-parapo">Ekiti Parapo</a>. In 1897 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/royal-niger-company-territories">Royal Niger Company</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> Suleiman, and Ilorin passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-of-northern-nigeria">Protectorate of Northern Nigeria</a>. Its emir still reigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwara-state">Kwara State</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1823 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.98%;width:1.47%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1823 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ilorin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdulsalami, Shita, Suleiman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yoruba, Fulfulde, Hausa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Ilorin, Ilorin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1860&amp;focus=ilorin-emirate" aria-label="Ilorin Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4806 1860 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ilorin Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5126 2116L5109 2141M5126 2116L5144 1947M5126 2116L5187 2202"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5109 2141h0M5144 1947h0M5187 2202h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5126 2116h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5126 2116h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1860&amp;focus=ilorin-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
